From 16d0e4225024bcc366b80491ba96b7f97f346220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Wallace <jwallace115@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 23:39:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] nfl_sim Phase 5A-7: 10-yard-zone KM outcome tables,
 empirical timeouts + kneel policy, measured safety rates

Cowork-executed. K1 pts/team 21.79 -> 22.49 (actual 22.39).

D27: pass/rush outcome tables at 10-yard zones (KM tail chained toward the
goal line; z5 parent as thin-cell fallback in the engine). Removes the 5A-4
0.687 deep-sack scale (y90/y100 cells carry measured sack yardage).
D28: timeout_policy + kneel_decision tables replace the 40-second /
"~1.5 opponent timeouts" kneel heuristic; timeouts are state (3 per half,
2 in OT) and switch the runoff to the stopped-clock kind. Late-half snaps,
timeouts and kneels now match reality.
D29: safety rates measured in build_constants by own-goal-line bucket;
hand-typed scaled values and two unused constants removed.

K1 definition correction: "pass yds" compared sack-inclusive actual with
sack-exclusive sim since Phase 2A; completion yards match (476.7 vs 474.2).
Remaining fails: volume (+4% drives), key-number mass (P(|m|=3) 7.7% vs
14.5%), FG att 3.56 vs 3.92. Tests: 59/61 (two spec failures reported red).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QMk9gfHmH2aTN5pwMcY52R
